# =============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file is the enforcement half of "centrally managed WAF". The priority
# bands and the exception rules are checked by the pipeline; this is what stops
# someone editing the central rules themselves.
#
# A pull request touching a path below cannot merge until an owner approves it,
# provided the branch protection rule on main has "Require review from Code
# Owners" enabled. WITHOUT THAT SETTING THIS FILE IS DOCUMENTATION, NOT A
# CONTROL. Check it before claiming the control exists:
#   Settings -> Branches -> main -> Require a pull request before merging
#                                -> Require review from Code Owners
#
# REPLACE THE PLACEHOLDER TEAM BELOW with the real GitHub team slug. A team
# that does not exist is silently ignored and nothing is enforced.
# =============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------- central WAF rules
# The mandatory rules and rate limits applied to every workload. An application
# team can add rules in band 70-100 through its own tfvars; it cannot reach
# these.
infrastructure/workload/central-rules.tf    @<org>/cloud-security

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the gate itself
# The band checks, the exception validation and the expiry enforcement. Someone
# who can edit these can grant themselves anything, so they belong to the same
# owners as the rules.
infrastructure/workload/exceptions.tf       @<org>/cloud-security
infrastructure/workload/variables.tf        @<org>/cloud-security

# --------------------------------------------------------------- the modules
# How a policy is rendered — scoped exclusions, rule set versions, the Front
# Door override handling.
infrastructure/modules/waf-policy-appgw/    @<org>/cloud-security
infrastructure/modules/waf-policy-afd/      @<org>/cloud-security

# ------------------------------------------------------------- this file
.github/CODEOWNERS                          @<org>/cloud-security

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT LISTED, ON PURPOSE: environments/*/workload.tfvars
#
# That is the application team's file. They own their own rules and their own
# exception requests, and they should be able to raise a pull request without
# waiting on security for a change that the pipeline already validates.
#
# Security's attention is a finite resource. Spending it on every tfvars edit
# means it is not available for the changes that actually matter.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
